      "writtenOn": "2021-10-05T17:25:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is just a personal UT philosophy of mine that doing the exact same math in the function under test and the test itself only verifies that bitwise operations are working. So instead I like to use known-good, pre-calculated test vectors because this would catch any arithmetic errors in the code. The comment is just to briefly describe where the value comes from to avoid magic numbers.",
      "parentUuid": "7e87e13d_2c37d987",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "06d2da79eda0be64727121a8f9e63619a88575b1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e29a44c_1c6d42ac",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/drivers/src/stm_mems_common.c",
