      "side": 1,
      "message": "I just tried removing it but we fail the test due to `Failed to find parameter val for mock_read_fn`. The problem is that since `st_write_data_with_mask()` does pass a valid / non-NULL output buffer to the read function, the logic I added to `mock_read_fn` on lines 29-32 expects an expected value to be supplied. I don\u0027t see a way in the ztest mocks to explicitly ignore such a param. `test_st_raw_read_n` works without this because a NULL pointer is passed in instead of an output buffer.\n\nI could either (1) leave this as is and add a comment clarifying that the \"read\" value is immaterial, or (2) come up with an alternate mechanism for enabling the output parameter, possibly using the arg parameter passed in when setting the mock.",
